From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Burker <burker@ucs.at>
Date: Tue, 07 Jul 2026 15:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drivers: wifi: esp32: keep interface dormant until associated

The esp32 Wi-Fi driver marks the network interface carrier-on at
WIFI_EVENT_STA_START, that is when the radio starts, not when the station has
associated with the access point. The interface therefore becomes
operational-up immediately, and the IPv6 stack runs Duplicate Address Detection
and its Router Solicitation burst (net_if.c, RS_COUNT = 3, one every
CONFIG_NET_IPV6_RS_TIMEOUT seconds) within the first ~2 seconds, while the link
is not yet usable. On Wi-Fi the association typically completes later, so every
solicitation is lost and the stack never solicits again. A global or ULA SLAAC
address then only appears when the router sends its next unsolicited Router
Advertisement, which can be tens of seconds later.

Gate the operational-up transition on association instead:
- mark the interface dormant at WIFI_EVENT_STA_START, before carrier-on, so it
  never flaps to up,
- clear dormant in the STA connect handler, which drives the operational-up
  notification and starts DAD and Router Solicitation at association time, and
- re-arm dormant in the STA disconnect handler so a later reassociation
  solicits again.

This mirrors the dormant handling used by other Zephyr Wi-Fi drivers and makes
the solicited Router Advertisement arrive right after association, so the SLAAC
address is obtained promptly instead of waiting for an unsolicited RA.
---
 drivers/wifi/esp32/src/esp_wifi_drv.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/wifi/esp32/src/esp_wifi_drv.c b/drivers/wifi/esp32/src/esp_wifi_drv.c
index d96c3bfd85d..b7e4d2f0c19 100644
--- a/drivers/wifi/esp32/src/esp_wifi_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/wifi/esp32/src/esp_wifi_drv.c
@@ -295,6 +295,11 @@ static void esp_wifi_handle_sta_connect_event(void *event_data)
 {
 	ARG_UNUSED(event_data);
 	esp32_data.state = ESP32_STA_CONNECTED;
+
+	/* Link is usable now. Clear dormant so the IPv6 stack runs DAD and Router
+	 * Solicitation at association time, not at radio start (STA_START).
+	 */
+	net_if_dormant_off(esp32_wifi_iface);
 #if defined(CONFIG_ESP32_WIFI_STA_AUTO_DHCPV4)
 	net_dhcpv4_start(esp32_wifi_iface);
 #else
@@ -306,6 +306,10 @@ static void esp_wifi_handle_sta_disconnect_event(void *event_data)
 {
 	wifi_event_sta_disconnected_t *event = (wifi_event_sta_disconnected_t *)event_data;

+	/* Link is down. Re-arm dormant so the next association triggers a fresh
+	 * Router Solicitation instead of leaving the interface operational-up.
+	 */
+	net_if_dormant_on(esp32_wifi_iface);
 	if (esp32_data.state == ESP32_STA_CONNECTED) {
 #if defined(CONFIG_ESP32_WIFI_STA_AUTO_DHCPV4)
 		net_dhcpv4_stop(esp32_wifi_iface);
@@ -427,6 +427,10 @@ void esp_wifi_event_handler(const char *event_base, int32_t event_id, void *event_data,
 	switch (event_id) {
 	case WIFI_EVENT_STA_START:
 		esp32_data.state = ESP32_STA_STARTED;
+		/* Keep the interface dormant until associated so the IPv6 stack does
+		 * not solicit routers on a link that is not yet usable.
+		 */
+		net_if_dormant_on(esp32_wifi_iface);
 		net_eth_carrier_on(esp32_wifi_iface);
 		break;
 	case WIFI_EVENT_STA_STOP:
--
